\ifsubmission
\emph{Measurement}: only one of the twelve studies in Table~\ref{tab:evidence} reports any model cost figure and none reports latency, data rate, bandwidth, or update strategy, so the same task should be benchmarked across device, gateway, and server placement with parameters, latency, and energy reported beside accuracy. \emph{Fusion}: no study reports performance with each modality withheld, so leave-one-modality-out evaluation at measured device failure rates is needed before a modality is judged to earn its cost. \emph{Explanation}: attention maps are offered as interpretability without faithfulness testing, which perturbation of the attended region against matched random regions would supply. \emph{Federation}: federated results are reported as single accuracy figures, without the rounds, bandwidth, energy, privacy budget, and local-only baseline that determine feasibility. \emph{World model twins}: no reviewed system meets both the action conditioning and the synchronization criterion and has been evaluated on outcomes, for which target trial emulation followed by silent mode deployment is the natural first test. \emph{Lifestyle}: our search surfaced no quantitative dietary or lifestyle study, so a cohort pairing clinical and continuous lifestyle streams is needed to test whether lifestyle context adds predictive information. \emph{Harmonization} and \emph{safety} complete the list: cross-site variation attributable to harmonization choices is unmeasured, and no study evaluates sensor spoofing, action label tampering, or planner manipulation for a twin permitted to act.
\fi



